===================Hadoop Intro and Architecture=====
key features of hadoop::
distributed storage and processing
Scalable and cost-effective
Fault-tolerant using data replication
High availability
Open-Source and community -driven

Hadoop Ecosystem (Core Components)::
HDFS (Hadoop Distributed File System) - storage layer
YARN (Yet Another Resource Negotiator) - Resource Management
MapReduce - Data processing framework
Hadoop Common - Shared utilities and libraries

Hadoop Architecture::
NameNode (Master): maintains metadata  (file name, permission, block locations etc)
DataNode (Slave): Stores actual data blocks and reports to the NameNode
Secondary NameNode: Assists NameNode by maintaining checkpoints (not the backup)
File are split into blocks (default 128MB) and replicated across multiple DataNodes.

YARN Architecture::
ResourceManager: Manages cluster resources globally
NodeManager: Manages resources on individual nodes
ApplicationMaster: Manages application execution
containers: Represent allocated resources (CPU and memory) 


MapReduce Processing Model::
MapReduce is a programming model used for parallel data processing. It works in two main phases: Map Phase processes input data, and Reduce Phase aggregates the output geenrated by the Map phase.

Advantages of Hadoop
Handles Very large datasets efficiently
Runs on commodity hardware
Reliable and fault-tolerant
Supports structured and unstructured data

Use Cases:
Log Processing and analysis
Data warehousing 
Recommendataion Systems
Fraud Detection
Social media analytics

